<title>SINGAPORE: Oman raises term May crude to $19.25/bbl - traders.</title>
<headline>Oman raises term May crude to $19.25/bbl - traders.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has raised its term lifting price for May crude to $19.25 per barrel from $17.53 in April, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Oman sets its prices on a retroactive basis.</p>
<p>Traders said the official selling price (OSP) meant that the Oman/Dubai differential has narrowed to 70 cents per barrel from 90 cents per barrel.</p>
<p>The differential is used as a guage of relative value between different crudes.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3199)</p>
